# Ordered gemini fallback chains, built 2026-08-13 directly off AI
# Studio's rate-limit dashboard (requests-per-minute / requests-per-day
# for each model, read live) after gemini-3.5-flash and
# gemini-3.5-flash-lite -- the only two models previously in rotation --
# both hit their daily caps from a self-message-echo-loop bug burning
# through quota before it was caught. Every model below shares the same
# API key/project, so they're genuinely separate quota buckets, same
# logic as the original two-model fallback this replaces.
#
# "main" (texts, curant-watcher's relay calls): ordered by reply quality
# first, newest/flagship models tried before older ones, so a customer
# text gets the best available model that still has quota. Deliberately
# does NOT prioritize by quota size -- a text is one request, not a
# multi-turn budget problem the way a live call is.
