# "fast" (live FaceTime calls, tier="fast" via curant-cli relay --
# distinct from curant-facetime-answerer.py's own GEMINI_CALL_MODEL_CHAIN
# used for transcription, which mirrors this ordering separately since
# it's a different process/SDK path): ordered by daily-quota depth
# first -- a multi-turn call can burn through a 20/day cap in one
# conversation, so the lite models with the deepest daily budgets
# (gemini-3.1-flash-lite and gemini-3.5-flash-lite, both 500 RPD) are
# tried before anything capped at 20/day, quality being a secondary
# concern for a low-latency relay leg.
#
# Left out deliberately: gemini-2-flash/gemini-2-flash-lite/gemini-2.5-pro
# (0/0 on this API key/project -- not enabled, would just fail
# immediately every time), and the Gemma 4 models (huge free quota --
# 30 RPM / 14.4K RPD -- but a different model family not confirmed to
